kangaroo-at-2020-kadett-16.body:
The three red faces of each little cube meet at one corner. In the $3 \times 3 \times 3$ cube:
- a corner cube shows 3 faces meeting at a corner: turn its red corner outwards;
- an edge cube shows 2 adjacent faces: two of its red faces can be turned outwards;
- a face-centre cube shows 1 face: turn a red face outwards;
- the centre cube is hidden.

So every visible little face can be red, and all 6 faces of the big cube are completely red.

**Answer: (E) 6**
